CHAPTER FOUR
4.1 SYSTEM IMPLEMENTATION AND TESTING
This chapter discusses the implementation and testing of the proposed Crime Reporting and Emergency Response System with Real-Time Location Tracking for Area Command Police Station, Auchi Division. It explains the development methodology, software and hardware requirements, implementation of the frontend and backend components, authentication mechanism, database integration, deployment process, and system testing. The system was developed using modern web and mobile application technologies to provide a secure, scalable, and user-friendly platform for crime reporting and emergency response. The frontend was implemented using Expo (React Native) with TypeScript, while the backend was developed using Node.js, Express.js, and MongoDB. Authentication was implemented using JSON Web Tokens (JWT), and the application was deployed on the Railway cloud platform. According to Adams (2021), selecting appropriate technologies significantly improves software performance, maintainability, and user experience. Similarly, Brown (2023) emphasizes that cloud-based architectures provide scalability and reliability for modern information systems.
