APPENDIX II
DATABASE COLLECTIONS
This appendix presents the MongoDB database collections used in the development of the Crime Reporting and Emergency Response System with Real-Time Location Tracking for Area Command Police Station, Auchi Division. The database consists of three primary collections: Users, Reports, and Emergencies. These collections are linked through the userId field to maintain relationships between users and their submitted reports or emergency alerts.
II.1 Users Collection
Collection Name: users
Description: Stores information about all registered users, including citizens and administrators.
Field Name	Data Type	Description
_id	ObjectId	Unique identifier for each user
fullname	String	User's full name
email	String	User's email address (Unique)
password	String	Encrypted user password
role	String	User role (Citizen or Admin)
createdAt	Date	Date the account was created
II.2 Reports Collection
Collection Name: reports
Description: Stores all crime reports submitted by registered users.
Field Name	Data Type	Description
_id	ObjectId	Unique report identifier
userId	ObjectId	References the user who submitted the report
title	String	Title of the crime report
description	String	Detailed description of the incident
latitude	Number	GPS latitude of the incident
longitude	Number	GPS longitude of the incident
status	String	Report status (Pending, In Progress, Resolved)
createdAt	Date	Date and time the report was submitted

II.3 Emergencies Collection
Collection Name: emergencies
Description: Stores emergency alerts submitted through the mobile application.
Field Name	Data Type	Description
_id	ObjectId	Unique emergency identifier
userId	ObjectId	References the user who sent the emergency alert
emergencyType	String	Type of emergency (Robbery, Fire, Accident, etc.)
latitude	Number	GPS latitude of the emergency location
longitude	Number	GPS longitude of the emergency location
status	String	Current status of the emergency
createdAt	Date	Date and time the emergency was reported

II.4 Relationship Between Collections
The relationship between the collections is illustrated below.
                  	 	 USERS
                      		      │
          ┌───────────┴───────────┐
          │                   				       │		
          │ 1          					        1..*
          │                      				       │
          ▼                       				       ▼
      REPORTS              		     EMERGENCIES
Relationship Description
•	One User can submit multiple Crime Reports. 
•	One User can submit multiple Emergency Alerts. 
•	The userId field in both the Reports and Emergencies collections references the _id field in the Users collection. 
•	This relationship ensures that every report and emergency alert is associated with a registered user, enabling efficient tracking and management of incidents. This database structure provides a scalable and organized approach to storing user information, crime reports, and emergency alerts while supporting secure data retrieval and efficient system operations.
